--- body ---
## Context

Promotion requested by the author (padme native-note triage, 2026-11-07; padme
smelt report `memory/smelts/2026-11-07-first-skill-smelt.md`). The Claude Code
native note `feedback_no_wrapper_skills.md` records the author's ruling of
2026-06-06 (padme PR #7 deleted three ticket wrapper skills): "/ticket-new,
/ticket-ready, /ticket-close should not exist at all. Our instructions should
be sufficient so that the smart model do erg new, erg ready and erg close."
A skill that adds no logic beyond invoking one self-documenting CLI is not
written; the direct invocation goes in the project instructions. Reason: KISS,
and wrappers drift (v1-era skills survived two format generations).
`rules/authoring-skills.md` does not cover it.

## Destination

`rules/authoring-skills.md`. Wording is the harness's call.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `rules/authoring-skills.md` says a skill that only wraps one
  self-documenting CLI is not created, and an existing one is proposed for
  deletion.
